---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "PelliScope Europe | Terms of use";
const description = "Terms for the PelliScope European website and services.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://pelliscope.eu/terms.html">
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content" class="legal-main">
    <section class="legal-hero section-shell">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span>European operation · Last updated 26 July 2026</p>
      <h1>Terms for the<br /><em>European service.</em></h1>
      <p>
        These terms govern the PelliScope European website and services operated by HawkFranklin OÜ.
        Country-specific clinical and consumer terms apply wherever a paid consultation service is available.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="legal-layout section-shell">
      <aside class="legal-summary">
        <strong>Current service status</strong>
        <p>Screening access and clinician consultation availability vary by country. Applicable prices, response ranges and refund terms are shown before payment.</p>
      </aside>
      <article class="legal-copy">
        <section>
          <h2>1. Operator</h2>
          <p>
            The European website and services are operated by HawkFranklin OÜ, registry code 17558108, Ahtri tn 12,
            15551 Tallinn, Estonia. Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@hawkfranklin.in">contact@hawkfranklin.in</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>2. Service availability</h2>
          <p>
            Access to screening, clinician response, consultation, prescription and payment functionality may vary by
            country and clinical pathway. A clinical service is available only where PelliScope identifies the relevant
            jurisdiction and pathway as active. Registration alone does not guarantee a clinician response or consultation.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>3. Screening, consultation and diagnosis</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Screening</strong> organises photographs and context and provides informational output.</li>
            <li><strong>Consultation</strong> begins only when a verified clinician accepts a case within an active service jurisdiction.</li>
            <li><strong>Diagnosis and treatment</strong> remain solely with the qualified clinician after professional review.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>PelliScope does not provide emergency care and its screening output must not be treated as medical advice or a diagnosis.</p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>4. User responsibilities</h2>
          <p>
            Users must provide information they are entitled to share, avoid submitting another person’s information
            without authority, follow capture guidance honestly and use the service lawfully. Do not delay urgent or
            in-person medical care because of a screening output or platform message.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>5. Clinician and community participation</h2>
          <p>
            Professional access is subject to identity, registration and jurisdiction checks. Community discussion is
            educational and does not itself create a treating-clinician relationship. A clinician remains responsible
            for practising within their competence, registration and applicable professional rules.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>6. Price, response and payment</h2>
          <p>
            There is currently no public EU patient consultation price and no clinician response-time guarantee. If a
            paid service launches, the total price, clinician details, issuing jurisdiction, expected response range,
            cancellation conditions and refund terms will be shown before payment.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>7. Intellectual property and acceptable use</h2>
          <p>
            The PelliScope name, interface and website content are protected by applicable intellectual-property law.
            You may not interfere with the service, bypass access controls, scrape protected clinical information,
            impersonate a clinician or use protected service data to train another system without written permission.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>8. Liability and governing law</h2>
          <p>
            The service is provided subject to mandatory law. Nothing in these terms
            excludes liability that cannot legally be excluded or limits mandatory consumer or patient rights. These
            terms are governed by Estonian law, while mandatory protections in a user’s country remain unaffected.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h2>9. Changes</h2>
          <p>
            These terms may be updated as country-specific clinical availability changes.
            Material new paid or clinical terms will be presented before a user enters that service.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
